  "question": {
    "text": "If the functions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math> have a common extreme point, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
